  "prefLabel": "Puc 1802.02 Application of Rules to Existing Buildings and Structures",
  "priorExpiration": "2015-07-31",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Puc 1802.02 Application of Rules to Existing Buildings and Structures. A change in occupancy or use of an existing building which would require an increase in demand for either fossil fuel or electrical energy supply to heat or cool the structure shall, pursuant to RSA 155-D:8, comply with the requirements of the energy code.\n\nSource. #6879, eff 2-1-99, EXPIRED: 2-1-07\n\nNew. #8811, INTERIM, eff 2-2-07, EXPIRED: 8-1-07\n\nNew. #8958, eff 7-31-07, EXPIRED: 7-31-15\n\nNew. #10908, eff 8-8-15",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/puc1800.html"
}
